# Serving and Streaming Rules

## Hard memory constraint
The whole Docker stack must fit in a 4GB Docker Desktop allocation on an 8GB
MacBook Air. Budget: Kafka ~1GB, FastAPI + model ~1GB, each consumer ~150MB.

## Consumers never load the model
Kafka consumers MUST NOT import torch or load a checkpoint. They call the
FastAPI service over HTTP. The model is loaded exactly once across the entire
stack. Do not suggest in-process inference "to avoid the HTTP hop" - it would
double the footprint and undo the decoupling.

## Kafka
- Official apache/kafka image, KRaft mode. No Zookeeper container ever.
- KAFKA_HEAP_OPTS=-Xmx512m -Xms512m
- Topic created with 3 partitions.
- Manual offset commit AFTER successful inference, never auto-commit. A crash
  mid-inference would otherwise silently drop a board.
- Undecodable images route to a dead-letter topic, they do not crash the
  consumer.
- Prefer natively multi-arch images (arm64 host).

## FastAPI
Load the model from the MLflow model registry by version, not from a
hardcoded checkpoint path.
